From 1929f5e16b059f9df706c9760b95c1c2060c1233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:50:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rpi-fbd: EDID polling, double buffering, screen blanking

Every 5 seconds rpi-fbd reads the EDID again; when it changes (a monitor
came, went or was replaced) it updates the connector and sends a hotplug
event. With room in the GPU memory it asks for two screens one below the
other, draws into the hidden one and moves the firmware visible window
to it. A client that sets no mode blanks the screen through the firmware.
